# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The build context is the REPO ROOT (the API is one workspace of an npm
# monorepo and needs the root lockfile plus packages/shared). Without this
# file that context would include node_modules and .git, which is hundreds of
# megabytes shipped to the daemon on every build for no reason.
#
# Rule of thumb: if the Dockerfile does not COPY it, it does not belong here.

# --- Dependencies: reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile ----------
# Critically, a host node_modules may contain platform-specific binaries
# (sharp's libvips in particular) built for macOS or arm64. Copying those
# into a linux/amd64 image produces a container that fails at import time.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# --- Build output: recompiled in the build stage ---------------------------
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- VCS -------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- Infrastructure and tooling: not part of the runtime image -------------
infra
scripts
.firebase
firebase.json
.firebaserc
firestore.rules
firestore.indexes.json
storage.rules
Makefile
.emulator-data

# --- Docs ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.md
LICENSE

# --- Secrets and local config ----------------------------------------------
# Belt and braces. Nothing in the deployed app reads a .env file (Cloud Run
# supplies the environment) and the API authenticates with ADC, so a key file
# should not exist at all -- but a stray one must never end up in a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
service-account*.json
*.pem
*.key

# --- Tests and coverage ----------------------------------------------------
coverage
**/*.test.ts
**/*.spec.ts
**/__tests__
vitest.config.ts

# --- The web app -----------------------------------------------------------
# The API image has no use for the React source. The web bundle is built on
# the host and deployed to Firebase Hosting.
# NOTE: apps/web/package.json is deliberately NOT excluded -- npm needs every
# workspace manifest present to resolve the workspace graph, and the
# Dockerfile copies it explicitly.
apps/web/src
apps/web/public
apps/web/index.html
apps/web/vite.config.ts
apps/web/tailwind.config.*
apps/web/postcss.config.*

# --- Editor and OS noise ---------------------------------------------------
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.log
.prettierrc*
.prettierignore
.eslintrc*
